#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111884 :tutorial/content "Let's recap some of the rules for exponents.\n\n- **Product rule**: to multiply powers of the same base, add the exponents.\n\n- **Quotient rule**: to divide powers of the same base, subtract the exponents.\n\n- **Power rule**: to raise a power to another power, multiply the exponents.\n\n- **Power of product rule**: to raise the product of two numbers to a power, raise each number to that power, and then multiply.\n\n- **Power of quotient rule**: to raise a fraction to a power, raise both the numerator and the denominator to that power.\n\nWe can use a combination of these rules to simplify expressions containing exponents. Let's see an example of this." :tutorial/id #uuid "7c442391-b257-5c16-9fe0-292a45e3c172" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3275 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
